{
  "context": {
    "answer": "Here's what's in `agent.xblox` — it's a **version 1 XBlox workflow file** (JSON format) with the following structure:\n\n---\n\n### `context` (stored state)\n| Key | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `answer` | A pre-stored LLM reply string |\n| `entries` | `[]` (empty list) |\n| `fps` | `0` |\n| `frames` | `0` |\n\n---\n\n### `roots` (pipeline nodes, in order)\n\n1. **`llmAgent`** — Calls an LLM with the prompt `\"whats in here ${CURRENT_FILE}\"`, streams the response, expects JSON back, and stores the result as `answer`. Tools are enabled (`\"tools\": true`).\n\n2. **`log`** — Logs an empty `info`-level message.\n\n3. **`fsList`** — Lists all files matching `${CURRENT_PATH}/*.*` and stores the result as `entries`.\n\n4. **`log`** — Logs the string `\"PREVIOUS\"` at `info` level.\n\n---\n\n**In short:** this is a test workflow that, when run against a file, asks an AI agent what's in it (with tool access), then lists all files in the current directory. The `context` block holds results from a previous execution — notably a cached `answer` where the agent incorrectly said tools were disabled.",
    "answer2": "",
